# crystalnoise3d

- Label: Crystal Noise 3D
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 45 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/crystalnoise3d.html
- Summary (EN): Produces crisp, faceted Worley-style noise sampled at each pixel's world-space position. It blends two randomly offset Worley noises for sharp angles, suited to rock patterns and chipping.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère un bruit de Worley anguleux en coordonnées monde 3D, adapté aux roches et aux éclats.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: sets output image size and metadata", "pos: optional RGB layer replacing the pixel world coordinates as the noise source", "time: optional layer giving a per-pixel time value"]

- Key parameters: ["Primary Metric: Euclidean, Manhattan or Chebyshev distance shaping the edges", "Jitter and Element Size: point displacement and cell size; Element Scale adjusts per axis", "Secondary: when on, primary settings drive the first noise and a second Metric, Jitter and Element Size set the second", "Flatten Faces: smooths faces so internal noise does not bulge", "Amplitude, Center, Noise Contrast: scale, offset and contrast before post-processing", "Offset: shifts the whole pattern in world space", "Post-processing (Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum): run in listed order"]

- Caveats: ["Negative values or values above 1 can occur; a Clamp COP can enforce range.", "Jitter above 1 can cause artifacts because points move past the search radius.", "Complement assumes 0 to 1 values and gives out-of-range results otherwise.", "Post-processing order changes the result."]

